      "problem": "A cube has a side length of $9\\,\\text{mm}.$ What is the volume of the cube?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the volume $V$ of a cube, we cube its side length. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =(9\\,\\text{mm})^{3} \\\\  & =9\\,\\text{mm}\\times 9\\,\\text{mm}\\times 9\\,\\text{mm} \\\\  & =(9\\times 9\\times 9)\\times (\\text{mm}\\times \\text{mm}\\times \\text{mm}) \\\\  & =729\\,{\\text{mm}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
